  "decision_conditions": [
    "Development under Class MA is permitted subject to the condition that it must be completed within a period of 3 years starting with the prior approval date. \r\t\t\rReason: To comply with the provisions of Part 3 of Schedule 2, Class MA of the GPDO the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) (Amendment) (No.2) Order 2020 And S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:\r\rDrawings:\r001A\r010C\r011C\r012B\r020\r030\r200\r100D\r101E\r102C\r300\rSupporting Information:\rNoise Impact Assessment Report VA5771.250306.NIA dated 10 March 2025\rDaylight & Sunlight Report dated 25th March 2025\rDesign & Access Statement dated March 2025\rTransport Statement STH-788-001-TS01 dated 26.09.2024\r\rReason: To ensure the development proceeds in accordance with the approved plans.\r",
    "Prior to the use commencing an acoustic report must be submitted to and approved by the local planning authority\rdemonstrating, by the performance of a sound insulation test, that the airborne sound attenuation of the separating floor between the proposed development and the commercial use has a minimum airborne sound insulation of DnT,w + Ctr \u0019$455dB.\rReason: To protect the residential amenity from noise and disturbance\r\r",
    "Prior to the occupation of the development, details of external lighting proposed shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The development shall be implemented in accordance with the approved details and shall be provided before the development is occupied. \r\rReason: to ensure that the development does not prejudice the amenities of adjoining occupiers and / or the visual amenities of the surrounding area and to ensure safe and appropriate light levels for access to units above.\r",
    "Prior to first occupation details of 6 secure cycle parking spaces have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details before it is occupied.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of cycle parking in line with the Council's adopted standards.\r",
    "Prior to first occupation, refuse storage facilities including facilities for the recycling of waste are to be provided within the development, in accordance with the Enfield Councils Waste and Recycling Planning Storage Guidance.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets.\r\r"
  ],
